    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Kyle Tucker** headlines the Austin Waves lineup with a 70.89 efficiency score, serving as our primary catalyst against Gasser. While the lefty-on-lefty matchup typically invites caution, **Kyle Tucker** maintains a high floor due to the wind blowing out at the park and his favorable spot in the heart of the order. Joining him in the outfield, **Andy Pages** (63.37) earns a strong recommendation primarily due to Gasser\u2019s slow delivery to the plate, which significantly increases the stolen base upside\u2014a critical factor given our aggressive pursuit of the SB category. Both players benefit from the environmental conditions, which helped nudge their base projections into the \"Strong\" start tier.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Luis Lara**, who just missed the cut with a 36.08 score. Despite the wind advantage, **Luis Lara** suffered from a poor matchup against Snell (3.22 xERA) and a suboptimal batting order placement, falling well below our 40.0 floor for active starters. Elsewhere, the roster remains thin; **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Jackson Merrill** are sidelined by a team off-day, and we continue to monitor the long-term status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains out on the IL. With **Gunnar Henderson**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Brayan Rocchio**, **Henry Bolte**, **Curtis Mead**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Franklin Arias**, **Dominic Smith**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Liam Hicks** also off the board due to the schedule, we are essentially leaning on our two active outfielders to carry the offensive production for the Waves today.",
